meta {
  name: Export (conditional, expect 304)
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

get {
  url: {{newBase}}/competitions/{{compId}}/export
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  If-None-Match: {{exportEtag}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 304
}

docs {
  Run "Export" first. This single 304 is the optional phase's whole argument: it says
  "nothing in this competition changed", replacing N conditional per-class requests.

  ~0.64 s here against ~2.5 s for 32 conditional class requests at concurrency 10.
  Requests drop 32 → 1, where 32 is simply the class count.

  The saving decays as `N / (1 + M)` with M classes changed, and on a tick where
  everything moved export is pure overhead — it wins because most competitions are
  idle on most ticks.
}
